	I have had to put together a script to ensure that the Tulip runs
correctly.  I had a similar problem in that the network would initialize
fine during system startup then 'die' when Linux loaded.  My workaround
is to reinstall the tulip.o driver with these parameters.  It works for
me:

/sbin/ifconfig eth0 down (take the interface down)
/sbin/rmmod tulip           (remove the tulip driver)
/sbin/insmod <where ever your tulip.o module is> options=14 (install with
options)
/sbin/ifconfig eth0 up     (bring the interface back up)

The options line loads the tulip driver with MII 100base Tx-FD as per
instructions found on the Scyld Computing Corporation site, an article on
"Linux and the Tulip NIC Architecture".  My tulip.o is in
/lib/modules/<kernel-version>/kernel/drivers/tulip/ and is the original
driver that came with the distribution.  The card is using the 21143
version of the chip.

Hope this helps,

MAB


