At the SRM (">>> ") prompt (sometimes called the "dead sargent"), issue
this command:

>>> SHOW *

...and watch for an environment variable called "console". If it is set
to "serial", there's one possibility. Connect to the COM1 port and try
again. 

Then again, it may very well be that the install kernel was set up for
serial console support instead of the graphics card.

First guess time... I'm obviously not a Linux/Alpha guy, but that may
soon change. I have years with Alphas (running OpenVMS), though...

