Jafir Elkurd <jafir.nospam@hotpop.nospam.com> wrote:
>> > I'd try boot dka100 -fl ""
>>
>> You better boot 'b dka100 -fl i', assuming that 'dka100' is indeed your
>> CD device, and type 'l' at 'aboot> ' prompt.  Read your screen and
>> follow that.  It is possible that with your graphics card you will be
>> better off with a "text" installation.
> 
> 
> When aboot loads, if you give it no flags, it will prompt you for which
> config to load.

This very much depends on what you happen to have in 'boot_osflags'
as they will be picked from there if not given explicitely.  Hence
'-flags i' as this guarantees an interactive aboot.  It is sane to
put there, for example, '0' and 'BOOT' in 'auto_action' to boot
automatically an entry 0 from your 'aboot.conf' on a power-up.

> if your flags are anything from 0-9 it will load that
> config.  and one of those (on the cd) is a serial install. (even if you are
> set to "graphics")

It is quite possible that 'text' install is good enough in this case
even without producing some kind of a serial console.  It is worth
to try.

   Michal


