The 3.x series generate faster code for Alpha than 2.95, in my
experience.  For some specific programs, 3.3 even beats ccc.  See some
posts by me a few weeks ago on that topic.  Make sure your gcc is
configured to optimize for your CPU.  If you built it yourself, it is
probably correct, otherwise it might be configured for ev45 by
default.

The main difference between -O2 and -O3 is automatic inlining of
functions, without an explicit 'inline' keyword.  Any higher number
than 3 is equivalent to 3.

